   "evidence": "scripts/lean_versions.py:14 `RELEASE_RE = re.compile(r\"\\Av(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)(?:-rc(\\d+))?\\Z\")` and :61 `return parsed is not None and parsed[0] == TRUSTED_MAJOR`; the comment at :54 states the premise (\"mathlib restricts `v4.*` tags to release managers\"). test_lean_versions.py:64 only exercises `v5.0.0`, `v3.9.0`, `v4.34.1-patch1`, so no leading-zero case is covered. Reached from bump_moves.decide:85 via `release_tag_of`, which gates the `release` kind in `mathlib_move` (bump_moves.py:52).",
   "file": "scripts/lean_versions.py",
   "fix": "Match the ruleset textually rather than numerically, e.g. `return parse_release(name) is not None and name.startswith(\"v4.\")`, or forbid leading zeros in `RELEASE_RE` (`v(0|[1-9]\\d*)\\.(0|[1-9]\\d*)\\.(0|[1-9]\\d*)`), which also stops `toolchain_order`/`why_not_newer` from reading `leanprover/lean4:v04.35.0` as a forward release in step 4. Add a `v04.34.1` case to `test_lean_versions.py:64` and to `test_check_bump.py`'s `test_only_v4_tags_count_as_releases`.",
   "issue": "`is_trusted_release_tag` claims to identify \"the tags mathlib's tag ruleset restricts to release managers and makes immutable\" (`v4.*`), but tests the *integer* major version, so names a `v4.*` glob does not match are accepted: `parse_release(\"v04.34.1\")` returns `(4, 34, 1, inf)`, hence `is_trusted_release_tag(\"v04.34.1\")` is True. That is the sole trust basis for the `release` move \u2014 mathlib off its nominated branch, off master, not a descendant \u2014 so the guard trusts a strictly larger tag set than the one it says is release-manager-only.",
   "line": 61
  }
 ],
